<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10979" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conventĭcŭlum</span></b> ,
		i, n.
		dim.
		conventus (rare). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>An assembly, meeting, association</i>: conventicula
			hominum, quae postea civitates nominatae sunt, <i><span class="en">Cic. Sest.
				42, 91</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">plebei urbanae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Dom. 28, 74</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A place of assembly</i>, <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 14,
				15</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ritus Christiani,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 15, 5, 31</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">27, 3, 13</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Arn. 4,
			152</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Lact. 5, 11, 10</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
